# Event-driven external waits

When CI or Jira work requires waiting, consume the signed webhook result from
the Redis event queue with `tools/agent-waiter/scripts/wait-for-event.mjs`.
Match the GitHub commit SHA and check name, or the Jira numeric issue ID and
target status ID. Pass a UTC `--after` timestamp captured before the external
operation. Do not poll GitHub or Jira, use `--watch`, or retry with sleep while
waiting. A missing event does not prove completion. The production webhooks are
configured at:

- `https://agent-waiter.vercel.app/api/github`
- `https://agent-waiter.vercel.app/api/jira`

Use the stored result as the completion signal. If the event store or delivery
fails, report that the outcome is unverified and repair the delivery path.
